  <title>Honne and Tatemae</title>
  <link>https://guitars.volumen.ca/posts/2026-06-21/</link>
  <description><![CDATA[ 




<p>Tempo: 85 bpm<br>
Score: <a href="honne_and_tatemae.pdf">Download</a><br>
MuseScore: <a href="honne_and_tatemae.mscz">Download</a></p>
<section id="video" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="video">Video</h2>
<p>80 bpm</p>
<div class="quarto-video ratio ratio-16x9"><iframe data-external="1" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/uUrcNmXqy-0" title="" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen=""></iframe></div>
<div class="quarto-video ratio ratio-16x9"><iframe data-external="1" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/mOIHlfyuIh0" title="" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen=""></iframe></div>
<div class="quarto-video ratio ratio-16x9"><iframe data-external="1" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/P2jbU3QC6wU" title="" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen=""></iframe></div>
<p>Just the Amp and Trem Pedal:</p>
<p>60 bpm</p>
<div class="quarto-video ratio ratio-16x9"><iframe data-external="1" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/TccAJh9Ursw" title="" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen=""></iframe></div>
<div class="quarto-video ratio ratio-16x9"><iframe data-external="1" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/Ko--WiylY4U" title="" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen=""></iframe></div>
<div class="quarto-video ratio ratio-16x9"><iframe data-external="1" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/IyfD4Sphpks" title="" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen=""></iframe></div>
<div class="quarto-video ratio ratio-16x9"><iframe data-external="1" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/UvvrcpthfsU" title="" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen=""></iframe></div>
<div class="quarto-video ratio ratio-16x9"><iframe data-external="1" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/E1TWdCgtcvE" title="" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen=""></iframe></div>
</section>
<section id="fender-telecaster" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="fender-telecaster">Fender Telecaster</h2>
<p>Pickup Position: Neck</p>
</section>
<section id="zoom-g3xn-on" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="zoom-g3xn-on">Zoom G3Xn ON</h2>
<p>106 Princeton</p>
</section>
<section id="joyo-tremolo-off" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="joyo-tremolo-off">Joyo Tremolo OFF</h2>
<p>Intensity: 50%<br>
Rate: 50%</p>
</section>
<section id="fender-blues-jr.-iii" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="fender-blues-jr.-iii">Fender Blues Jr.&nbsp;III</h2>
<p>Volume: 4.5<br>
Fat: OFF<br>
Treble: 5.5<br>
Bass: 4.5<br>
Middle: 5.0<br>
Master: 4.5<br>
Reverb: 1.0</p>
</section>
<section id="blue-yeti" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="blue-yeti">Blue Yeti</h2>
<p>Gain: 9 o’clock<br>
Mode: Cardioid mode, 4” from speaker, slightly off-axis</p>
</section>
<section id="dolby-on" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="dolby-on">Dolby ON</h2>
<p>OFF</p>
</section>
<section id="zoom-g3xn-princeton-patch-checklist" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="zoom-g3xn-princeton-patch-checklist">Zoom G3Xn “Princeton” Patch Checklist</h2>
<p><strong>Guitar</strong>: Fender Telecaster MIJ, neck pickup, Master Volume ~9, Master Tone ~9<br>
<strong>Zoom</strong>: G3Xn, Firmware 2.20, Patch cell 106, Patch name “Princeton” Goal: Warm, articulate Princeton Reverb-style clean tone with shimmer trem and spring reverb<br>
<strong>Amp</strong>: Fender Blues Jr III (real amp, miked — no Zoom amp/cab sim used)</p>
<section id="signal-chain" class="level3">
<h3 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="signal-chain">Signal Chain</h3>
<p>Guitar → RackComp → RC Boost → Tremolo → FD Spring → Zoom output → Blues Jr input → mic</p>
<p>Note: guitar Volume/Tone currently near max (<sub>9/</sub>9) rather than rolled back. Brighter/more aggressive than original plan — if tone feels too bright or aggressive once recorded, roll Tone back to 6-7 as first adjustment.</p>
</section>
<section id="block-1-rackcomp-dynamics" class="level3">
<h3 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="block-1-rackcomp-dynamics">Block 1 — RackComp (DYNAMICS)</h3>
<ul class="task-list">
<li><label><input type="checkbox" checked="">THRSH: 25</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox" checked="">Ratio: 3</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox" checked="">ATTCK: 5</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox" checked="">VOL: 100 (unity/pass-through — not a boost like RC Boost’s Volume)</label></li>
</ul>
</section>
<section id="block-2-rc-boost-drive" class="level3">
<h3 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="block-2-rc-boost-drive">Block 2 — RC Boost (DRIVE)</h3>
<ul class="task-list">
<li><label><input type="checkbox" checked="">Gain: 15</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox" checked="">Bass: 50</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox" checked="">Treble: 55</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox" checked="">VOL: 65 (adjusted down from 100/max after A/B testing — 100 was a noticeable level jump, not a subtle push)</label></li>
</ul>
</section>
<section id="block-3-tremolo-modulation" class="level3">
<h3 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="block-3-tremolo-modulation">Block 3 — Tremolo (MODULATION)</h3>
<ul class="task-list">
<li><label><input type="checkbox" checked="">Wave: <strong>TUBE</strong></label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox" checked="">Depth: 35</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox" checked="">Rate: 30</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox" checked="">VOL: 100</label></li>
</ul>
</section>
<section id="block-4-fd-spring-reverb-sole-reverb-source-option-a" class="level3">
<h3 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="block-4-fd-spring-reverb-sole-reverb-source-option-a">Block 4 — FD Spring (REVERB) — sole reverb source (Option A)</h3>
<ul class="task-list">
<li><label><input type="checkbox" checked="">Active: ON</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox" checked="">Color: 1</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox" checked="">Lo: 55</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox" checked="">Hi: 45</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox" checked="">Mix: 30</label></li>
</ul>
<p>Decision: FD Spring is the sole <em>meaningful</em> reverb source. Blues Jr’s physical Reverb dial has no true zero (range is 1–12), so it stays at its physical minimum (1) — this contributes a negligible touch of onboard spring underneath and is not treated as problematic stacking.</p>
</section>
<section id="block-5-rhythm-rhythm-and-looper-practice-aid-not-part-of-the-recorded-tone" class="level3">
<h3 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="block-5-rhythm-rhythm-and-looper-practice-aid-not-part-of-the-recorded-tone">Block 5 — Rhythm (RHYTHM AND LOOPER) — practice aid, not part of the recorded tone</h3>
<ul>
<li><label><input type="checkbox" checked="">Active: ON (intentional — metronome for practice)</label></li>
<li>Pattern: Metro4 4/4</li>
<li>Volume: 4</li>
<li><strong>Reminder: disable or mute before any actual take</strong> — this is a metronome click, not a tone-shaping effect, and isn’t meant to bleed into the final recording</li>
</ul>
</section>
<section id="amp-settings-blues-jr-iii-dials-112-no-true-zero" class="level3">
<h3 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="amp-settings-blues-jr-iii-dials-112-no-true-zero">Amp Settings — Blues Jr III (dials 1–12, no true zero)</h3>
<ul class="task-list">
<li><label><input type="checkbox" checked="">Volume: 4.5</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox" checked="">Fat: OFF</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox" checked="">Treble: 5.5</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox" checked="">Bass: 4.5</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox" checked="">Middle: 5.0</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox" checked="">Master: 4.5</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox" checked="">Reverb: 1 (physical minimum — FD Spring on the Zoom is the sole meaningful reverb source, see Block 4)</label></li>
</ul>
</section>
<section id="mic-setup-blue-yeti-on-stock-desktop-stand-floor-placement" class="level3">
<h3 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="mic-setup-blue-yeti-on-stock-desktop-stand-floor-placement">Mic Setup — Blue Yeti (on stock desktop stand, floor placement)</h3>
<ul class="task-list">
<li><label><input type="checkbox">Mode: Cardioid</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox">Orientation: <strong>logo side of mesh grille facing the amp</strong> (this is the capsule’s listening face — confirmed correct)</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox">Distance: 4–5 inches from grille</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox">Position: base shifted slightly to the <strong>right</strong> of the amp’s centerline (creates true off-axis angle, since the stock stand doesn’t swivel sideways)</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox">Tilt: forward, toward the amp — this aims the capsule up to cone height (compensating for the stand sitting lower than the speaker on the floor)</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox">Gain: set using the <em>loudest</em> tremolo peak, target -12 to -6 dB, no clipping</label></li>
</ul>
<p>Notes: - Forward tilt = vertical aim adjustment (reaches cone height), not the off-axis angle - Sideways base offset = true off-axis angle (softens pick attack/harshness) - Both adjustments are used together in this floor setup since the stand can’t swivel independently</p>
</section>
<section id="test-pass" class="level3">
<h3 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="test-pass">Test Pass</h3>
<ul class="task-list">
<li><label><input type="checkbox">Turn OFF/mute Rhythm (metronome) block before recording an actual take</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox">Record 15–20 seconds of comping/chords</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox">RC Boost check: at Volume 65, should feel like a mild lift, not an obvious pedal jump. Adjust down further (55–60) if still too pushed.</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox">Reverb check: FD Spring is the sole meaningful reverb source (amp Reverb sits at its physical minimum of 1) — confirm the overall reverb amount feels right, not doubled</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox">Tremolo check: TUBE wave should feel smoother/rounder than a standard triangle wave trem</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox">Compression check: RackComp should be felt as sustain/evenness, not obvious pumping</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox">Guitar tone check: Volume/Tone near max (<sub>9/</sub>9) — if the result feels too bright/aggressive, roll Tone back to 6–7 first</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox">Overall: does the amp feel like it’s “working” a little (natural compression) rather than stiff/clean?</label></li>
<li><label><input type="checkbox">If still too clean/stiff: raise Master first, before touching EQ</label></li>
</ul>


</section>
</section>

